                    <p>
                        The second article in BET KANU Magazine, featured in The Mesopotamian Influence edition, examines the world’s earliest known legal systems: the Code of Ur-Nammu, the Code of Lipit-Ishtar, and the Laws of Eshnunna. The article explores the circumstances of their discovery, their structural composition, and their foundational legal principles, while also analyzing their profound influence on the later Code of Hammurabi
                    </p>
